sockets/ - TCP/UDP demos for AmigaPython 2.7
===========================================

Require bsdsocket.library (Roadshow or similar).  Start the stack first.

Kept:

  broadcast.py    UDP broadcast time
  radio.py        Receive broadcasts from broadcast.py
  unicast.py      UDP to localhost
  udpecho.py      UDP echo client/server
  echosvr.py      Simple TCP echo server
  throughput.py   TCP throughput test
  finger.py       Finger client (port 79; service often absent)
  ftp.py          Minimal FTP client
  rpython.py      Remote Python client
  rpythond.py     Remote Python server (insecure; demo only)

Removed: AF_UNIX (unixclient/unixserver), fork-based telnet.py,
multicast/regsub mcast.py, Unix-shell gopher.py.

Also see ../chatserver.py for a multi-user TCP chat demo.

Example (two Shells, stack running):

  Python echosvr.py
  Python -c "import socket; s=socket.socket(); s.connect(('127.0.0.1',7)); s.send('hi\n'); print s.recv(100)"
